{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker"]},{"title":"Analytics","anchor":"Analytics","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/AnalyticsValue","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every screen that models its state with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":" already knows exactly when it was opened and when it moves between Empty, Loading, Data, and Error. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" turns those moments into "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent"},{"type":"text","text":"s and fans them out to as many "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker"},{"type":"text","text":"s as you register — one per analytics backend (Firebase, Mixpanel, Amplitude, your own logging endpoint, a debug console print, …)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates ships no backend-specific tracker implementations, so the core module stays dependency-free — but it does include "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" (logs every event to the console) and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" (silently discards everything), so you don’t have to hand-roll a console logger just to confirm events fire at the right moments. For a real backend, write one small adapter, converting the event’s backend-agnostic "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/AnalyticsValue"},{"type":"text","text":" parameters into that SDK’s own format:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct FirebaseScreenTracker: ScreenAnalyticsTracker {","    func track(_ event: ScreenAnalyticsEvent) {","        Analytics.logEvent(event.name, parameters: event.parameters.mapValues { value in","            switch value {","            case .string(let string): string","            case .int(let int): int","            case .double(let double): double","            case .bool(let bool): bool","            }","        })","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An adapter is also free to remap "},{"code":"event.name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to whatever vocabulary its backend expects — Firebase, for example, reserves a specific constant for screen views."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Wiring a screen","level":2,"anchor":"Wiring-a-screen"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let analytics = ScreenAnalyticsService(trackers: [FirebaseScreenTracker(), PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker()])","","func onAppear(source: ScreenOpenSource<AppScreen>) {","    analytics.trackScreenOpened(\"Articles\", source: source.analyticsKind)","    analytics.observeStateChanges(of: store, screen: \"Articles\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"trackScreenOpened(_:source:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends one "},{"code":"screen_opened","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" event. "},{"code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the same "},{"code":"withObservationTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" mechanism "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},{"type":"text","text":" uses to mirror a store, and sends a "},{"code":"screen_state_changed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" event for every subsequent "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":" transition — call it once, right where you create or first observe the store. When a transition lands on "},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the event also carries the error’s "},{"code":"localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It also times how long the screen spends in "},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the moment the state leaves "},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", it sends a "},{"code":"screen_load_duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" event ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenLoadDuration(screen:outcome:milliseconds:)"},{"type":"text","text":") with that outcome and the elapsed time in "},{"code":"duration_ms","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — useful for a “how long do loads actually take, and how often do they end in an error” dashboard without hand-rolling a stopwatch around every "},{"code":"load(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"screen_state_changed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" event landing on "},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tells you a screen failed to load; it doesn’t tell you whether the user gave up or hit Retry. Call "},{"code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenRetryTapped(screen:)"},{"type":"text","text":") from the same "},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure you pass to the Error placeholder, so that’s a distinct, countable event instead of indistinguishable from the screen’s initial "},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateView(store.state, onRetry: {","    analytics.trackRetryTapped(\"Articles\")","    Task { await store.load { try await api.fetchArticles() } }","}) { articles in","    ArticleList(articles)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadNextPage(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t move "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" off "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on either a success or a failure, so "},{"code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has nothing to report for it — call "},{"code":"trackNextPageLoaded(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"trackNextPageFailed(_:errorDescription:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenNextPageLoaded(screen:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenNextPageFailed(screen:errorDescription:)"},{"type":"text","text":") from the same place you call "},{"code":"loadNextPage(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mirroring how "},{"code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called from "},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func loadMore() async {","    await store.loadNextPage { try await api.fetchArticles(page: nextPage) }","    if let error = store.loadNextPageError {","        analytics.trackNextPageFailed(\"Articles\", errorDescription: error.localizedDescription)","    } else {","        analytics.trackNextPageLoaded(\"Articles\")","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.Scre